cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, its pipeline or its schemas, please cite it."
title: "Operational Context Corpus for Autonomous Systems"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible corpus linking real telemetry from autonomous systems to the
  external operating conditions under which it was produced, with a queryable
  schema and full provenance. Its first result is an agreement analysis between
  ERA5 reanalysis wind and onboard PX4 EKF2 wind estimates over 871 flights. The
  analysis plan and its decision thresholds were fixed before any result existed;
  two statistical summaries and the pooled weighting were corrected afterwards,
  recorded as post-hoc. The finding: no evidence of a systematic component-wise
  offset, and agreement too imprecise for the reanalysis to substitute for the
  onboard estimate. An operational-design-domain
  representation is in scope and not yet built.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/AndreaBozzo/occas"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22127669"
identifiers:
